%U A382452 977777777880595,9777777778805796,97777777788057797,977777777880577798,9777777778805777799,97777777788057777800,977777777880577777802
%N A382452 Number of self numbers <= 10^n.
%C A382452 Let F(t) be the number of nonnegative integers v such that t = v + s(v), where s(v) is the decimal digit sum of v. Thus t is a self (Colombian) number iff F(t)=0. By Theorem 7 of Alekseyev and Sloane, if t = c*(10^m+1) + k is the canonical representation, then F(t) = F(k) + F(9*m-k-2), with F(r) = 0 for r < 0. Hence the self-number indicator in a decimal block can be computed from arguments of size O(m), making it possible to determine a(n) for large n. - _Max Alekseyev_, Sep 16 2026
